# The commands ngspice's grammar lists as inert in its control language (run, quit) are left
# out with a note; any other command (print) is an error that names the language it is of.
from: ngspice
to: xyce
--- input
t
R1 a 0 1k
.control
op
run
print v(a)
quit
.endc
.end
--- output
t
R1 a 0 1k
.op
* [sprack] not written: print v(a)
.end
--- report
info[oneway]: line 3: script: xyce has no control script; the ngspice script's analyses and outputs are written as the netlist's own, in order
info[loss]: line 5: simctl: 'run' is not written: a netlist for xyce runs its analyses without it
error[unsupported]: line 6: simctl: 'print v(a)' is a command of ngspice's control language and cannot be written for xyce: Xyce has no control language besides its dot commands
info[loss]: line 7: simctl: 'quit' is not written: a netlist for xyce runs its analyses without it
